                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Map the convergence and the value migration`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `It is 5 May 2026. A hardware-agnostic energy OS has launched and two utilities are bundling it. Using Hacklin’s lens on technological convergence, decide <strong>where value is actually migrating</strong> — it is leaving the box and moving to the <em>energy-and-data layer</em> on top of it. Identify which Helvetia Climatec asset is <strong>defensible</strong> (the 240,000 installed units, the installer trust, the brand) versus <strong>exposed</strong> (the hardware margin), and quantify the EBIT at risk: roughly <em>CHF 20–24M a year</em> if the box commoditizes to 6–7%. Diagnose first — you cannot reel in value you have not located.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Reconfigure the business model`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Move beyond “sell a better box.” Redesign <strong>how</strong> Helvetia Climatec creates, delivers and captures value — toward recurring revenue. The strongest reconfiguration is <em>climate-as-a-service</em>: energy optimization and predictive maintenance <strong>anchored on the 240,000 installed units</strong>, an asset no software entrant can replicate. A pure software pivot with no defensible asset is just a narrative against a player with 50 million users. And the 1,200 independent installers your subscription disintermediates are also your <em>moat</em> against the platform — turn them into casualties and you arm your own disruptor.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Pick the partner ecosystem`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `The founding-partner tier closes this round. Choose among four postures: <strong>component supplier</strong> inside the dominant platform (fast, but they own the customer, data and recurring revenue), a <strong>utility-led open alliance</strong> (share the layer, keep the relationship), a <strong>proprietary Helvetia OS</strong> (full control, but a CHF-heavy race under your cap), or a <strong>European manufacturer coalition</strong> (scale). Mid-round a key Swiss utility threatens to go exclusive with the rival — your ecosystem must survive a partner defection. Read the <em>lock-in</em>: the easy choice can cement the very commoditization it was meant to escape.`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Reallocate R&D and defend the plan`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `The board will not raise the <strong>CHF 38M R&D cap</strong>. Every franc shifted to software, connectivity and energy-services R&D must be <em>cut from legacy hardware</em> — the two boxes must sum to 38 or less, or it is a wish list, not a reallocation. The realistic software need is around <strong>CHF 14M</strong>. Then deliver the 3-minute defense: prove the reconfiguration, the ecosystem choice and the R&D shift <em>protect and grow group EBIT</em>, not just chase a software story. The board is activist-leaning and wants the EBIT number, not the vision slide.`,

