                    insight_captured:       `Convergence captured: you reconfigured the model onto climate-as-a-service anchored on the 240,000 installed units, chose an ecosystem that kept the customer relationship, and funded the shift inside the CHF 38M cap by genuinely cutting hardware. Value migrated up the stack — and so did you. Value-capture rose, group EBIT held and grew, and the installer moat survived.`,
                    insight_box:            `Defended the box: you invested in a better hardware endpoint while value migrated to the energy-and-data layer. The platform sits on top of your improved box and takes the recurring margin; your value-capture of the new layer was capped and EBIT kept eroding toward 6–7%. You optimized the layer value was leaving.`,
                    insight_lockin:         `Locked in: you joined the dominant platform as a component supplier without reading the lock-in, so the platform owns the customer, the data and the recurring revenue. You escaped commoditization by signing up for it — a capped value-capture and a platform tax on a 6% box.`,
                    insight_narrative:      `Narrative without asset: you pivoted to “the energy software company” without anchoring on the defensible installed base. Against a global platform with 50 million users you had aspiration, not an edge — and EBIT bled funding a story rather than reeling value onto a real asset.`,
                    insight_proprietary:    `Over-ambitious platform: you committed to the proprietary Helvetia OS without the R&D headroom the cap allows to fund it. The most ambitious ecosystem play is also the most resource-fragile — years from earning, capped recurring revenue, and a race against a player spending ten times your budget.`,
                    insight_paper:          `Paper reallocation: you claimed to shift R&D to the migrating value while breaching the CHF 38M cap or protecting every legacy hardware program. A reallocation you won’t fund by cutting something is a wish list — the new model stayed unfunded and value-capture was capped.`,
                    insight_channel:        `Channel revolt: you disintermediated the 1,200 installers who are your distribution moat against the platform. They became opponents rather than the service-and-data channel, weakening the ecosystem and the recurring base just when you needed them most.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A mixed reconfiguration: parts of the plan reeled value in, but the model, ecosystem and R&D reallocation didn’t fully reinforce each other — enough seams for commoditization risk to persist and for the board to question whether group EBIT is really protected.`,
                    insight_ebit_low:       `Group EBIT was not protected: the transition consumed more margin than the new recurring value replaced, leaving the activist-leaning board the very evidence it feared — a software story that did not defend the number.`,
